diff --git a/third/ggpo/CVF_CHANGES.txt b/third/ggpo/CVF_CHANGES.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e75abd5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/third/ggpo/CVF_CHANGES.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+github.com/ikemen-engine/ggpo v0.0.0-20260914163559-279d7303151f (the version
+Ikemen GO 6a09392 requires), used through a replace in go.mod. Copied without
+its tests, example/, internal/mocks/, README, logo and go.sum; go.mod is
+unchanged, so the module graph is the same.
+
+CvF Online change (internal/protocol/protocol.go, marked "CvF Online"):
+the sync handshake survives packet loss. Timing only: packet formats and
+everything after synchronization are unchanged, and it plays against builds
+without the change.
+
+- A lost sync request or reply is retransmitted after 200 ms (was 2 s), with
+  the same random as before, so a late reply to an earlier copy still counts
+  even when the round trip is longer than 200 ms. The retry timer is its own
+  (lastSendTime also moves with replies to the peer's requests).
+- A peer that has synchronized waits at least 15 s (was DisconnectTimeout,
+  3 s in Ikemen) without packets before it drops the other, as long as the
+  other has sent nothing but sync requests/replies (it may still be
+  synchronizing, e.g. an older build that retries every 2 s), and it reports
+  no interruption meanwhile. Once the other sends anything else (inputs,
+  keep-alives, quality reports) the configured timeouts apply as before.
